[{'id': 40666, 'title': None, 'body': '<p>If I get this right you want a vector that is normal to the screen plane but in world coordinates?</p> <p>In that case you want to <code>INVERT</code> the transformation from <code>World -&gt; Screen and do Screen -&gt; World</code> of <code>(00-1)</code> or <code>(001)</code> depending on which axis the screen points down.</p> <p>Since the ModelView matrix is just a rotation matrix (ignoring the homogeneous transformation part) you can simply pull this out by taking the transpose of the rotational part or simple reading in the bottom row - as this transposes onto the <code>Z</code> coordinate column under transposition.</p>', 'accepted_answer_id': None, 'answer_count': None, 'comment_count': 0, 'community_owned_date': 'NaT', 'creation_date': '2008-09-02 21:05:56.027000+00:00', 'favorite_count': None, 'last_activity_date': '2016-02-20 16:39:00.497000+00:00', 'last_edit_date': '2016-02-20 16:39:00.497000+00:00', 'last_editor_display_name': None,


